			<div class="content" id="post-content-2227657">
									

<p>This isn't especially helpful. I see this type of comment fairly often, and it doesn't qualify as criticism of the piece. It's criticism of how people are reading the piece. If you're going to tell people they're missing the point, provide some under-the-cut clarification of your viewpoint so we can have an actual discussion about it. This just smacks of &quot;you're doing it wrong, people who downvoted&quot;.</p>
<p>I don't care for the tone here, I don't care for the over-extended list of hijinks, the requisite knowledge of staff characters in order to get the (in my opinion) rather bland jokes, and I feel the trickster mythos isn't treated with quite the level of complexity I would expect. That's why I downvoted, and that's my opinion. So if you're going to tell me I'm missing something integral, shed a little light on your own opinion why this rises above the interpretations of others, please.</p>

